# The LF-only gate (`line-endings`) and every suite that mutates a source file
# by exact LF text require these to be LF in the working tree. The machine's
# global `core.autocrlf=true` rewrote lane patches to CRLF (measured 2026-11-24:
# the gate refused `twitch-adblock.js` and `content.js`), so the dialect is
# pinned here instead of being re-normalized by hand after every merge.
kick-overlay/*.js text eol=lf
kick-overlay/*.cjs text eol=lf
kick-overlay/*.json text eol=lf
kick-overlay/*.html text eol=lf
kick-overlay/*.css text eol=lf
_tools/*.mjs text eol=lf
_tools/*.json text eol=lf
# `_tools/ko-replica/*` is a second level, and it was left out: measured
# 2026-11-26, `server.mjs` and `run.mjs` came back from an isolated lane as
# CRLF while HEAD stores LF, so the next `git checkout` would rewrite them and
# an exact-text edit would miss. One pattern per level is the bug; globstar is
# the fix.
_tools/**/*.mjs text eol=lf
_tools/**/*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
# `*.gitattributes` itself is not product code, but the machine's autocrlf had
# already rewritten it once in this repo; pin it so a checkout cannot split the
# diff of a one-line rule into every line of the file.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
# The revival artifacts are written by Python (`json.dumps` + `\n`) and read
# back by their own gates (`feature_map_sync --gate`, `benchmark_history --gate`,
# `loop_friction_audit measure --gate`). Measured 2026-11-26: without this pin,
# `git add features/features.json` warned "LF will be replaced by CRLF", so the
# next checkout would hand the gate a CRLF document while the writer assumes LF.
features/*.json text eol=lf
features/*.md text eol=lf
benchmarks/*.json text eol=lf
benchmarks/*.jsonl text eol=lf
revival/*.json text eol=lf
revival/*.md text eol=lf
revival/*.jsonl text eol=lf
harness/*.json text eol=lf
harness/*.tsv text eol=lf
